Nothing is left for this phase. The assessment brief ends with "write, commit, then STOP. Do not write task files. Do not implement anything", so I haven't started on any of the problems I found.

session_plan/assessment.md is on disk (71 lines, about 9.5 KB) and has all nine required sections, plus a "Suggested priority for the planner" section at the end. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refuses it and the brief's || true lets that pass. I didn't force-add it, because the ignore rule looks deliberate and the planner reads the file straight from disk. The working tree has no other changes.

The planner's next pass should pick from these three, in this order:
1. **Ctrl+C-style flush for SIGTERM:** when a piped `-p` run is killed with SIGTERM, everything it was holding is lost (0 bytes, against 4920 bytes when killed with SIGINT). My own loop's timeout kills hit this. #991 doesn't mention it, so it needs a new issue or an explicit note on #991.
2. **`yoyo map "dir sp"`:** a folder with a space in its name can't be mapped at all (exit 2). This is the next harmful one in #1009.
3. **yoyo watch at the shell:** it prints "Watch mode ON" and exits 0, but the setting dies with that one process, so it reports success while doing nothing.

One constraint for whatever gets planned: src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 15 lines from the size limit. A task that adds more than that without splitting the file or adding it to the exception list will fail cargo test and be reverted.
